{"id":"a1f6d4733dbaf832","group":"58","path":"58/batch16/58-df-energy-functional.md","title":"Energy Functional","display":"df-energy-functional — Energy Functional","type":"definition","metadata":{"type":"definition","book":"Set Theory","book_abbrev":"58","label":"58-df-energy-functional","aliases":["58-df-energy-functional","Energy Functional"],"display":"df-energy-functional — Energy Functional","depends_on":["[[58-df-sobolev-space]]","[[58-df-function]]","[[58-df-weak-derivative]]","[[58-df-bochner-integral]]","[[58-df-test-function]]"]},"metadataError":null,"renderWarnings":[],"properties":[{"key":"type","html":"definition"},{"key":"book","html":"Set Theory"},{"key":"book_abbrev","html":"58"},{"key":"label","html":"58-df-energy-functional"},{"key":"aliases","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span>58-df-energy-functional</span><span>Energy Functional</span></div>"},{"key":"display","html":"df-energy-functional — Energy Functional"},{"key":"depends_on","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-1\" data-note=\"38c58fda0da62833\" href=\"?note=38c58fda0da62833\" title=\"58-df-sobolev-space\">58-df-sobolev-space</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-2\" data-note=\"36d7463d215be751\" href=\"?note=36d7463d215be751\" title=\"58-df-function\">58-df-function</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-3\" data-note=\"03ca577eb4c1b05e\" href=\"?note=03ca577eb4c1b05e\" title=\"58-df-weak-derivative\">58-df-weak-derivative</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-4\" data-note=\"9e0348ed2298c600\" href=\"?note=9e0348ed2298c600\" title=\"58-df-bochner-integral\">58-df-bochner-integral</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-5\" data-note=\"458fd0dccec3665f\" href=\"?note=458fd0dccec3665f\" title=\"58-df-test-function\">58-df-test-function</a></span></div>"}],"html":"\n<h2 id=\"Hypothesis\">[Hypothesis]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"n\\in\\omega\\setminus\\{0\\}\">\\(n\\in\\omega\\setminus\\{0\\}\\)</span>, <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\Omega\\subseteq\\mathbb R^n\">\\(\\Omega\\subseteq\\mathbb R^n\\)</span>, and <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"H,J,u,v,w,z,q,r\\in V\">\\(H,J,u,v,w,z,q,r\\in V\\)</span></li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{SobolevSpace}_S(H,\\Omega,n,1,2)\">\\(\\mathrm{SobolevSpace}_S(H,\\Omega,n,1,2)\\)</span> (the real <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"W^{1,2}\">\\(W^{1,2}\\)</span> carrier)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\operatorname{WeakDerivative}_S\">\\(\\operatorname{WeakDerivative}_S\\)</span> and <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{BochnerIntegral}_S\">\\(\\mathrm{BochnerIntegral}_S\\)</span> (weak derivative and signed scalar integral predicates)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathcal B_\\Omega,\\mu_\\Omega\">\\(\\mathcal B_\\Omega,\\mu_\\Omega\\)</span> (Borel sigma algebra and restricted Lebesgue measure on <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\Omega\">\\(\\Omega\\)</span>)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathcal B_{\\mathbb R},+_{\\mathbb R},\\cdot_{\\mathbb R},|\\cdot|\">\\(\\mathcal B_{\\mathbb R},+_{\\mathbb R},\\cdot_{\\mathbb R},|\\cdot|\\)</span> (standard real measurable and normed-space data)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathcal D(\\Omega)=C_c^\\infty(\\Omega)\">\\(\\mathcal D(\\Omega)=C_c^\\infty(\\Omega)\\)</span> (test-function space)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{WeakGradient}_S,\\mathrm{DirichletEnergyValue}_S,\\mathrm{EnergyFunctional}_S,\\mathrm{EnergyFirstVariation}_S,\\mathrm{EulerLagrange}_S\">\\(\\mathrm{WeakGradient}_S,\\mathrm{DirichletEnergyValue}_S,\\mathrm{EnergyFunctional}_S,\\mathrm{EnergyFirstVariation}_S,\\mathrm{EulerLagrange}_S\\)</span> (predicates defined here)</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"Assertion\">[Assertion]</h2>\n<figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{df\\text{-}energy\\text{-}weak\\text{-}gradient}\\vdash\\mathrm{WeakGradient}_S(w,u,\\Omega,n)\\leftrightarrow\\mathrm{Function}(w,n,L^2(\\Omega))\\land\\forall i\\in n\\;\\operatorname{WeakDerivative}_S(w(i),u,e_i,\\Omega,n),\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\mathrm{df\\text{-}energy\\text{-}weak\\text{-}gradient}\\vdash\\mathrm{WeakGradient}_S(w,u,\\Omega,n)\\leftrightarrow\\mathrm{Function}(w,n,L^2(\\Omega))\\land\\forall i\\in n\\;\\operatorname{WeakDerivative}_S(w(i),u,e_i,\\Omega,n),\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{df\\text{-}energy\\text{-}value}\\vdash\\mathrm{DirichletEnergyValue}_S(r,u,\\Omega,n)\\leftrightarrow\\exists w,q\\in V\\;\\Bigl(\\mathrm{WeakGradient}_S(w,u,\\Omega,n)\\land\\mathrm{Function}(q,\\Omega,\\mathbb R_{\\geq0})\\land\\forall x\\in\\Omega\\;\\bigl(q(x)=\\sum_{i\\in n}w(i)(x)^2\\bigr)\\land\\mathrm{BochnerIntegral}_S(r,q,\\Omega,\\mathcal B_\\Omega,\\mu_\\Omega,\\mathbb R,\\mathcal B_{\\mathbb R},\\mathbb R,+_{\\mathbb R},\\cdot_{\\mathbb R},|\\cdot|)\\Bigr).\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\mathrm{df\\text{-}energy\\text{-}value}\\vdash\\mathrm{DirichletEnergyValue}_S(r,u,\\Omega,n)\\leftrightarrow\\exists w,q\\in V\\;\\Bigl(\\mathrm{WeakGradient}_S(w,u,\\Omega,n)\\land\\mathrm{Function}(q,\\Omega,\\mathbb R_{\\geq0})\\land\\forall x\\in\\Omega\\;\\bigl(q(x)=\\sum_{i\\in n}w(i)(x)^2\\bigr)\\land\\mathrm{BochnerIntegral}_S(r,q,\\Omega,\\mathcal B_\\Omega,\\mu_\\Omega,\\mathbb R,\\mathcal B_{\\mathbb R},\\mathbb R,+_{\\mathbb R},\\cdot_{\\mathbb R},|\\cdot|)\\Bigr).\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{df\\text{-}energy\\text{-}functional}\\vdash\\mathrm{EnergyFunctional}_S(J,\\Omega,n,H)\\leftrightarrow\\mathrm{SobolevSpace}_S(H,\\Omega,n,1,2)\\land\\mathrm{Function}(J,H,\\mathbb R_{\\geq0})\\land\\forall u\\in H\\;\\mathrm{DirichletEnergyValue}_S(J(u),u,\\Omega,n).\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\mathrm{df\\text{-}energy\\text{-}functional}\\vdash\\mathrm{EnergyFunctional}_S(J,\\Omega,n,H)\\leftrightarrow\\mathrm{SobolevSpace}_S(H,\\Omega,n,1,2)\\land\\mathrm{Function}(J,H,\\mathbb R_{\\geq0})\\land\\forall u\\in H\\;\\mathrm{DirichletEnergyValue}_S(J(u),u,\\Omega,n).\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{df\\text{-}energy\\text{-}first\\text{-}variation}\\vdash\\mathrm{EnergyFirstVariation}_S(r,u,v,\\Omega,n)\\leftrightarrow\\exists w,z,q\\in V\\;\\Bigl(\\mathrm{WeakGradient}_S(w,u,\\Omega,n)\\land\\mathrm{WeakGradient}_S(z,v,\\Omega,n)\\land\\mathrm{Function}(q,\\Omega,\\mathbb R)\\land\\forall x\\in\\Omega\\;\\bigl(q(x)=2\\sum_{i\\in n}w(i)(x)z(i)(x)\\bigr)\\land\\mathrm{BochnerIntegral}_S(r,q,\\Omega,\\mathcal B_\\Omega,\\mu_\\Omega,\\mathbb R,\\mathcal B_{\\mathbb R},\\mathbb R,+_{\\mathbb R},\\cdot_{\\mathbb R},|\\cdot|)\\Bigr).\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\mathrm{df\\text{-}energy\\text{-}first\\text{-}variation}\\vdash\\mathrm{EnergyFirstVariation}_S(r,u,v,\\Omega,n)\\leftrightarrow\\exists w,z,q\\in V\\;\\Bigl(\\mathrm{WeakGradient}_S(w,u,\\Omega,n)\\land\\mathrm{WeakGradient}_S(z,v,\\Omega,n)\\land\\mathrm{Function}(q,\\Omega,\\mathbb R)\\land\\forall x\\in\\Omega\\;\\bigl(q(x)=2\\sum_{i\\in n}w(i)(x)z(i)(x)\\bigr)\\land\\mathrm{BochnerIntegral}_S(r,q,\\Omega,\\mathcal B_\\Omega,\\mu_\\Omega,\\mathbb R,\\mathcal B_{\\mathbb R},\\mathbb R,+_{\\mathbb R},\\cdot_{\\mathbb R},|\\cdot|)\\Bigr).\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{df\\text{-}energy\\text{-}euler\\text{-}lagrange}\\vdash\\mathrm{EulerLagrange}_S(u,\\Omega,n,H)\\leftrightarrow\\mathrm{SobolevSpace}_S(H,\\Omega,n,1,2)\\land u\\in H\\land\\forall v\\in\\mathcal D(\\Omega)\\;\\mathrm{EnergyFirstVariation}_S(0,u,v,\\Omega,n).\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\mathrm{df\\text{-}energy\\text{-}euler\\text{-}lagrange}\\vdash\\mathrm{EulerLagrange}_S(u,\\Omega,n,H)\\leftrightarrow\\mathrm{SobolevSpace}_S(H,\\Omega,n,1,2)\\land u\\in H\\land\\forall v\\in\\mathcal D(\\Omega)\\;\\mathrm{EnergyFirstVariation}_S(0,u,v,\\Omega,n).\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><h2 id=\"Remark\">[Remark]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>The Euler--Lagrange clause is the weak harmonic equation against compactly supported smooth variations; minimization requires separate boundary data and admissible-class hypotheses.</li>\n<li>Weak gradients and both integrals carry their Sobolev, measure, measurable-space, and scalar structure explicitly; the unrelated Dirichlet-series dependency has been removed.</li>\n<li>Harmonic maps: minimize energy between manifolds; Euler-Lagrange from variations</li>\n<li>Calculus of variations: extremals solve Euler-Lagrange equations; natural boundary conditions</li>\n<li>Ginzburg-Landau: <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"F_\\epsilon(u) = \\int (|\\nabla u|^2/2 + V(u))\">\\(F_\\epsilon(u) = \\int (|\\nabla u|^2/2 + V(u))\\)</span>; minimizers approach vortices</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"Reference\">[Reference]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Evans, Partial Differential Equations</li>\n<li>Dacorogna, Introduction to the Calculus of Variations</li>\n</ul>\n","headings":[{"id":"Hypothesis","text":"[Hypothesis]","level":2},{"id":"Assertion","text":"[Assertion]","level":2},{"id":"Remark","text":"[Remark]","level":2},{"id":"Reference","text":"[Reference]","level":2}],"links":[{"target":"58-df-sobolev-space","status":"resolved","id":"38c58fda0da62833","anchor":"ref-1","targetAnchor":"","location":"元